# SDR Type 01h - Full Sensor Record owned by a *non-BMC* controller reached
# over a *non-zero* channel, at a *non-zero* LUN.
#
# Every other record in tests/transcripts/sensor.tr has owner ID 20h, LUN 0 and
# channel 0, which leaves three things unpinned:
#
#   * `keys.lun`      = byte [7] bits 1:0 -> req.msg.lun of Get Sensor Factors
#                       and of Set Sensor Thresholds;
#   * `keys.channel`  = byte [7] bits 7:4 -> the channel argument of
#                       ipmi_sdr_get_sensor_thresholds();
#   * BRIDGE_TO_SENSOR(), which only fires when the owner/channel pair differs
#     from intf->target_addr / intf->target_channel.
#
# Byte [7] is 5Dh = 0101 1101b: channel 5, FRU owner LUN 3, sensor owner LUN 1.
# Three different non-zero fields, so a wrong mask or a wrong shift changes the
# logged request.  In particular the FRU owner LUN bits are set, which is what
# separates the sensor owner LUN's `& 3' from a `& 7' or a `& 0xf'; a keys byte
# of 51h would leave all three indistinguishable.  See the "distinct, non-zero
# bytes" rule in tests/transport/Bmc.zig.

9c a3        # [1:2]  Record ID = 0xa39c
51           # [3]    SDR version 1.5 (51h)
01           # [4]    Record type 01h = Full Sensor Record
30           # [5]    Record length = 48 bytes follow

2c           # [6]    Sensor owner ID 2Ch (not the BMC's 20h)
5d           # [7]    Sensor owner LUN 1, FRU owner LUN 3, channel 5
77           # [8]    Sensor number 77h
0a           # [9]    Entity ID 10 = Power Supply
09           # [10]   Entity instance 9
7f           # [11]   Sensor initialization
68           # [12]   Sensor capabilities: thresholds readable+settable
02           # [13]   Sensor type 02h = Voltage
01           # [14]   Event/reading type 01h = threshold
ff 3f        # [15:16] Assertion event mask / lower threshold reading mask
ff 3f        # [17:18] Deassertion event mask / upper threshold reading mask
3f 3f        # [19:20] Settable / readable threshold mask (all six thresholds)
00           # [21]   Units 1: analog format 0 (unsigned)
04           # [22]   Units 2: base unit 04h = Volts
00           # [23]   Units 3: no modifier unit
00           # [24]   Linearization: linear
03           # [25]   M = 3 (LS 8 bits)
09           # [26]   M MS 2 bits = 0, tolerance = 9
f2           # [27]   B = -14 (LS 8 bits of the 10-bit two's complement 3F2h).
             #        A negative B is what lets a small raw threshold convert to
             #        a negative value, which is the only way to reach the
             #        `if (val[i] < 0) val[i] = 0` clamp in the validator.
c0           # [28]   B MS 2 bits = 11b | accuracy LS 6 bits = 0
00           # [29]   Accuracy MS | accuracy exp | sensor direction
f0           # [30]   R exponent = -1, B exponent = 0.  Dividing by ten puts the
             #        lower non-recoverable threshold at -0.5 rather than -11,
             #        i.e. strictly between -1 and 0, so `val[i] < 0' and
             #        `val[i] < -1' disagree.
07           # [31]   Analog flags: nominal, normal max and normal min specified
1e           # [32]   Nominal reading = 30
46           # [33]   Normal maximum = 70
0c           # [34]   Normal minimum = 12
ff           # [35]   Sensor maximum reading = 255
00           # [36]   Sensor minimum reading = 0
64           # [37]   Upper non-recoverable = 100
5a           # [38]   Upper critical = 90
50           # [39]   Upper non-critical = 80
0a           # [40]   Lower non-recoverable = 10
14           # [41]   Lower critical = 20
1e           # [42]   Lower non-critical = 30
0b           # [43]   Positive-going threshold hysteresis
0e           # [44]   Negative-going threshold hysteresis (differs from positive)
00 00        # [45:46] Reserved
00           # [47]   OEM
c5           # [48]   ID string type/length: 8-bit ASCII, 5 characters
42 72 64 67 53   # [49:53] "BrdgS"
